0903.5444	open_problem	Methods for guaranteeing hard bounds on the control inputs, within our context, while ensuring tractability of the underlying optimization problem are, to our knowledge, not available in the current literature.	In this article we solve the problem of stochastic receding horizon control for linear systems subject to additive (possibly) unbounded disturbances and hard norm bounds on the control inputs, over a class of feedback policies. Methods for guaranteeing hard bounds on the control inputs, within our context, while ensuring tractability of the underlying optimization problem are, to our knowledge, not available in the current literature. Preliminary results in this direction were reported in [ HCL09 ].	0.9
