1112.0343	future_work	While the current approaches yield exponentially large non-recursive Datalog programs, it is possible to rewrite queries and TBoxes into non-recursive Datalog programs whose size is simultaneously polynomial in the query and the TBox.	We plan to investigate rewriting and optimization techniques for sticky-join sets of TGDs, and alternative forms of rewriting such as positive-existential queries. We also plan to develop improved techniques for rewriting an ontological query into a non-recursive Datalog program, rather than into a union of conjunctive queries (recall the discussion in Section 2). While the current approaches yield exponentially large non-recursive Datalog programs, it is possible to rewrite queries and TBoxes into non-recursive Datalog programs whose size is simultaneously polynomial in the query and the TBox. This will be dealt in a forthcoming paper.	0.95
