quant-ph/0402095	open_problem	Are R_1(f) and Q_1(f) polynomially related for every total Boolean function f? Also, can we exhibit any asymptotic separation between these measures?	• Are R_1(f) and Q_1(f) polynomially related for every total Boolean function f? Also, can we exhibit any asymptotic separation between these measures? The best separation we know of is a factor of 2: for the equality function we have R_2(EQ) 2 (1 - o(1)) log n, whereas Winter [37] has shown that Q_1(EQ) 2 (1/2 + o(1)) log n using a protocol involving mixed states. This factor-2 savings is tight for equality: a simple counting argument shows that Q_1(EQ) 2 (1/2 - o(1)) log n; and although the usual randomized protocol for equality [31] uses (2 + o(1)) log n bits, there exist protocols based on error-correcting codes that use only log(cn) = log n + O(1) bits. All of this holds for any constant error probability 0 <  < 1/2.	0.9
